Type: Agents must close the tasks they finish, not only refrain from closing
  ones they have not
Request-or-TODO: User: "also in the agent file, always tell the agent to mark
  completed todos if its using a todo list"
Outcome: AGENTS.md carried only the guard -- never mark an item complete before
  its output exists and its verification passes -- which reads as a reason to
  leave boxes unchecked. The Task Lifecycle now states the other half: when
  working from a task list, whether TODOS.md or an ephemeral session list, mark
  each item as it lands rather than in a batch at the end, check the box in the
  same commit as the work, and record the evidence beneath it. Finished work
  under an unchecked box is indistinguishable from work nobody started, and the
  next agent redoes it or routes around it. Work finished that the list does not
  contain gets its item added and checked in the same commit
