Change-ID: CL-20260802-018
Commit: pending
Date: 2026-08-02
Type: The coordinator binds a fixed loopback port instead of an ephemeral one
Request-or-TODO: User: "so for the dev server tell it to keep teh port stable
  and try to use this port 47311"
Outcome: codeflux start now defaults to 127.0.0.1:47311 instead of
  127.0.0.1:0, exported as DefaultListenAddress. codeflux-dev serve inherits it,
  since it shells to start without an address. An explicit --address still wins,
  and the coordinator library keeps its :0 default so tests continue to take
  ephemeral ports and run in parallel. A fixed port also makes a stale server
  visible: the bind now fails with a message naming the likely cause and the
  --address escape, where the ephemeral default silently gave every abandoned
  server a port of its own and nothing ever collided
Affected-behavior: codeflux start binds 47311 by default. A second coordinator
  cannot start while the first holds the port; that is the intended behaviour
